{"scenario":"bad-deploy","description":"payment v2.4.1 ships a card tokenizer bug (+ an unrelated catalog deploy as a red herring)","mode":"graph","recorded_at":"2026-10-18 05:50","duration":68.02,"agent":{"duration_s":43.6,"tool_calls":9,"cost_usd":0.13330060000000002,"input_tokens":93263,"output_tokens":2639,"report":"The alert is resolved: a bad payment deploy was breaking checkout. I rolled payment back and frontend errors dropped to 0% within about 7 seconds. The incident is INC-043, now resolved, with recovery time about 0.4 minutes.\n\n**Root cause:** the payment deploy from v2.4.0 to v2.4.1 (`chg-deaf9c1f`, a \"saved-card tokenization refactor\" by riya), which went out 11 seconds before the alert. The new code crashes in `card_tokenizer.tokenize` with `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not subscriptable` when a request has no card details. This is the same bug that caused INC-031 12 days ago.\n\n**Evidence path:** frontend (16% errors) \u2192 checkout (failing only because payment was) \u2192 **payment** (75% errors, 39 of 52 failures raised inside payment itself; the services it depends on were healthy).\n- **Logs:** payment's logs show only one error, 28 repeats of the TypeError above, at `card_tokenizer.py:88`, all on v2.4.1.\n- **History:** payment's runbook RB-PAY-01 says to roll back when this error follows a release; there is no feature flag to turn off instead. INC-031 was the same error and was fixed with a rollback.\n- **Ruled out:** catalog was also deployed (v3.0.4 \u2192 v3.1.0) 14 seconds before the alert, but it stayed healthy, so it wasn't the cause.\n\n**Action (1 of 3 allowed):** I ran a dry run of the rollback first, then rolled payment back to v2.4.0 (new deploy `chg-061c8631`).\n\n**Verification:** frontend went from 10.2% errors (degraded) to 0% (healthy) on the next two checks. p95 latency is about 110ms.\n\n**Paged:** riya, on call for the payments team, in #team-payments. No webhook is configured, so the page was only recorded in the graph and never actually sent. Someone needs to contact riya directly.\n\n**Follow-up:** add a null check for saved cards in `card_tokenizer`, plus a test for it, before v2.4.1 goes out again.","start_t":11.48,"end_t":55.52},"events":[{"t":0.05,"kind":"start","text":"healthy baseline"},{"t":3.11,"kind":"inject","text":"payment v2.4.1 ships a card tokenizer bug (+ an unrelated catalog deploy as a red herring)"},{"t":11.48,"kind":"alert","text":"ALERT frontend error rate 16%, p95 116ms"},{"t":11.48,"kind":"agent","text":"headless agent started (graph mode)"},{"t":55.52,"kind":"done","text":"agent finished"}],"steps":[{"t":17.26,"n":1,"tool":"rank_suspects","note":"top suspect payment (score 0.999) via path frontend -> checkout -> payment","targets":["Service:catalog","Service:checkout","Service:frontend","Service:payment","Runbook:RB-PAY-01","Incident:INC-031","Change:chg-68d8f84b","Change:chg-deaf9c1f"]},{"t":18.77,"n":2,"tool":"get_logs","note":"read 29 log entries of payment","targets":["Service:payment"]},{"t":19.19,"n":3,"tool":"find_similar_incidents","note":"3 similar past incidents, best INC-031","targets":["Incident:INC-019","Incident:INC-027","Incident:INC-031"]},{"t":22.87,"n":4,"tool":"open_incident","note":"INC-043: Frontend errors: payment v2.4.1 card_tokenizer TypeError","targets":["Incident:INC-043"]},{"t":23.81,"n":5,"tool":"get_blast_radius","note":"blast radius of payment: 2 upstream, 1 downstream","targets":["Service:checkout","Service:fraud-check","Service:frontend","Service:payment"]},{"t":23.81,"n":6,"tool":"rollback_service","note":"DRY RUN rollback payment v2.4.1 -> v2.4.0","targets":["Service:payment","Change:chg-deaf9c1f"]},{"t":26.4,"n":7,"tool":"get_blast_radius","note":"blast radius of payment: 2 upstream, 1 downstream","targets":["Service:checkout","Service:fraud-check","Service:frontend","Service:payment"]},{"t":27.02,"n":8,"tool":"rollback_service","note":"ROLLED BACK payment v2.4.1 -> v2.4.0","targets":["Service:payment","Change:chg-d